<small>A Song of degrees.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Blessed <i>is</i> every one that feareth the LORD; that walketh in his ways.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy <i>shalt</i> thou <i>be</i>, and <i>it shall be</i> well with thee.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> Thy wife <i>shall be</i> as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the LORD.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> The LORD shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s children, <i>and</i> peace upon Israel. <br />
